    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"# Prioritized Experience Replay (PER) - Empirische Untersuchung\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## Überblick\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Dieses Assignment untersucht **Prioritized Experience Replay (PER)** empirisch durch:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Konzeptionelle Erklärung von PER\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Vergleich: Uniform Replay vs. PER\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Training mit beiden Methoden\\n\",\n",
    "    \"4. Detaillierte Visualisierungen und Analyse\\n\",\n",
    "    \"5. Reflexion und Interpretationen\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"## TEIL 1: KONZEPTIONELLE ERKLÄRUNG\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
    "  {\n",
    "   \"cell_type\": \"markdown\",\n",
    "   \"metadata\": {},\n",
    "   \"source\": [\n",
    "    \"### 1.1 Der Replay Buffer - Funktionsweise\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Warum brauchen wir Experience Replay?**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"In Deep Reinforcement Learning sammelt der Agent Erfahrungen sequenziell:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Aufeinanderfolgende Transitions sind stark korreliert\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Training mit korreliertem Daten ist ineffizient und instabil\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Die Gradienten werden \\\"verrauscht\\\" und divergieren\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Lösung: Experience Replay**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Speichere alle (s, a, r, s', done) Transitions in einem Buffer\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Sample zufällig aus diesem Buffer für Training\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Bricht Korrelation auf → stabileres Training\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Traditioneller Uniform Replay Buffer:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Buffer = [Transition1, Transition2, ..., TransitionN]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Sampling: random.sample(Buffer, batch_size)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Jede Transition hat gleiche Wahrscheinlichkeit\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- Einfach, aber nicht optimal!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### 1.2 Prioritized Experience Replay (PER) - Das Problem mit Uniform Sampling\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Problem:** Nicht alle Transitions sind gleich wertvoll für das Lernen!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Beispiel:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **\\\"Überraschende\\\" Transitions**: TD-Error war groß → Agent hat diese schlecht vorhergesagt\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- **\\\"Langweilige\\\" Transitions**: TD-Error war klein → Agent kennt diese schon\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Intuition:** Lernen geschieht schneller, wenn wir uns auf Fehler konzentrieren!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Beispiel:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Transition A: Q_predicted = 5.0, Q_actual = 5.1  → TD-Error = 0.1 (klein, langweilig)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Transition B: Q_predicted = 2.0, Q_actual = 8.0  → TD-Error = 6.0 (groß, wichtig!)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Uniform Replay: Beide werden mit 50% Wahrscheinlichkeit gesamplet\\n\",\n",
    "    \"PER:            B wird häufiger gesampelt (proportional zu TD-Error)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### 1.3 Wie funktioniert PER?\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Schritt 1: Priorität basierend auf TD-Error**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"priority_i = |TD_error_i| + ε\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"wobei:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- TD_error = R + γ * max Q(s', a') - Q(s, a)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- ε = kleine Konstante (verhindert priority = 0)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Schritt 2: Sampling-Wahrscheinlichkeit**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"P_i = priority_i^α / Σ(priority_j^α)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"wobei:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- α ∈ [0, 1] = Priorität-Parameter\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- α = 0: Uniform Sampling (alle Wahrscheinlichkeiten gleich)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- α = 1: Volle Priorität (linear nach TD-Error)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Schritt 3: Importance Sampling Weights (ISW)**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Problem: Sampling mit Prioritäten ändert die Datenverteilung → verzerrtes Lernen!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Lösung: Gewichte (Importance Sampling Correction)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"weight_i = (N * P_i)^(-β)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"wobei:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- N = Buffer-Größe\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- β ∈ [0, 1] = Bias-Korrektur-Parameter\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- β = 0: Keine Korrektur (PER mit voller Bias)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- β = 1: Volle Korrektur (unbiased)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"- weight werden normalisiert: weight_i /= max(weight)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Beispiel mit Zahlen:**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Angenommen 4 Transitions im Buffer:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Transition 1: priority = 1.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Transition 2: priority = 2.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Transition 3: priority = 3.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Transition 4: priority = 4.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Total Priority = 10.0\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Mit α = 0.6:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"P(sample 1) = 1.0^0.6 / (10.0) = 0.1\\n\",\n",
    "    \"P(sample 2) = 2.0^0.6 / (10.0) = 0.15\\n\",\n",
    "    \"P(sample 3) = 3.0^0.6 / (10.0) = 0.22\\n\",\n",
    "    \"P(sample 4) = 4.0^0.6 / (10.0) = 0.27\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Mit β = 0.4:\\n\",\n",
    "    \"weight_1 = (4 * 0.1)^(-0.4) = 1.74\\n\",\n",
    "    \"weight_2 = (4 * 0.15)^(-0.4) = 1.39\\n\",\n",
    "    \"weight_3 = (4 * 0.22)^(-0.4) = 1.15\\n\",\n",
    "    \"weight_4 = (4 * 0.27)^(-0.4) = 1.00  (max weight, wird 1.0 nach Normalisierung)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"→ Höher gesampelte Transitions bekommen kleinere Gewichte!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"---\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"### 1.4 SumTree - Effiziente Implementierung\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Problem:** Normales Sampling ist O(n) - zu langsam!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"**Lösung: SumTree Datenstruktur**\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\\n\",\n",
    "    \"        [10]           ← Root (Summe aller Prioritäten)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"       /    \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"      [6]   [4]        ← Innere Knoten\\n\",\n",
    "    \"     / \\\\    / \\\\\\n\",\n",
    "    \"    [1][5][3][1]       ← Blätter (Transitions)\\n\",\n",
    "    \"\\n\",\n",
    "    \"Sampling: \\n\",\n",
    "    \"1. Generiere random Zahl s ∈ [0, 10]\\n\",\n",
    "    \"2. Traverse vom Root: Wenn s <= left_child.sum → gehe links, sonst rechts\\n\",\n",
    "    \"3. Komplexität: O(log n) statt O(n)!\\n\",\n",
    "    \"```\"\n",
    "   ]\n",
    "  },\n",
